
(a) Objectives: how they were considered
Objective formulation used in your current code (what you’ve implemented)

You’re solving a capacitated p-median-type problem where a solution is a set of p facility locations (medians) chosen among customer sites, and customers are assigned to open facilities.

You evaluated each candidate median set with two objectives:

Cost

f1(x) = Σ_i distance(i, assigned_median(i))
(You set demand_weighted=False to match the benchmark scale; demands are used only for capacity feasibility.)

Distance is Euclidean floored to integer, i.e. floor(sqrt(dx^2 + dy^2)).

Capacity violation

f2(x) = Σ_m max(0, load(m) − capacity)
where load(m) is total assigned demand to median m.

This makes it a bi-objective constrained optimization:

feasible solutions have f2 = 0

infeasible solutions have f2 > 0



