Capacity constraint: how it was addressed
What your current decoder does (be explicit)

Your evaluation uses a greedy assignment decoder:

Customers are processed in desc_demand order (largest demand first)

Each customer is assigned to the nearest feasible median (one that still has capacity)

If none has remaining capacity, assign to the nearest anyway and count violation later

So constraint handling has two layers:

Decoder tries to satisfy capacity (feasibility-first assignment choice)

Any remaining overload is measured as violation and minimized via the algorithm